I have made a small change (r8187b_endpoint-12.patch) on top of a patch whi=
ch
Herton (rtl8187b_5.patch) sent to Axel for a new mac80211-based driver for =
Realtek
8187B. Herton's patch was missing one thing that the vendor driver does - t=
he vendor
driver sends management control frames through usb endpoint 12 rather than =
the normal
priority-based queueing endpoints 6,7,5,4. Without the management frame cha=
nge, it
seems that the new driver can scan but not associate, and my patch fixes th=
at. My patch
is probably a bit ugly (hence I have not provided an integrated patch), but=
 since it is
just a few lines and short enough, I am sure somebody can re-write it bette=
r.

So I *am* using the new driver *right now* connected to the internet...

The rest of the story is at:
https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=3D432280

These two patches are the same as (and Herton may have a newer/better one f=
or his already):
https://bugzilla.redhat.com/attachment.cgi?id=3D304231
https://bugzilla.redhat.com/attachment.cgi?id=3D305203

